\subsection*{Piezo-Ceramic Actuated Boundary Layers}

Embedded lead zirconate titanate (PZT) micro-actuators within thrust chamber
walls counter-act acoustic pressure oscillations at frequencies up to
\(50 \,\text{kHz}\).

\subsection*{Topological Stress Dissipation}

Channels carved into the outer jacket follow minimal-surface geometries
(Gyroid and Schwarz P-surfaces) to distribute mechanical shock evenly across
multi-directional vectors.

